    {
      "id": 873577,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A flaw in Node.js Permission Model enforcement can over-grant filesystem access across radix-tree prefix boundaries.\n\nUnder `--permission`, an attacker who is granted access to one path can abuse boundary handling to read from or write to paths outside the intended filesystem allowlist.\n\nThis vulnerability affects Node.js **main**, **22.x**, **24.x**, and **26.x**.",
